From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:58:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: bring the J604 GPU work back onto
 Aurora's driver

2d2ca1559a took Aurora's GPU driver whole, which dropped the J604's
G16 work that had applied cleanly on integration/aurora. Ten of those
commits are carried again unchanged before this one; the rest of the
work, which builds on the series' integration snapshot, is merged here
file by file onto Aurora's driver and Aurora's deep-sleep path:

- the J604 board and firmware admission (qualified_board with the
  J604's own firmware list), the PMP telemetry lease check;
- the governor's idle floor as a runtime parameter, with the J604's
  S1 floor after an idle stretch;
- TA before FS record order (g16_ta_first), the adjustable completion
  repoll, a render command published behind a running one
  (g16_flights), reuse of a leased PB manager of the same VM by
  default, same-queue dependents reaching the engine early;
- the sysfs values of the runtime parameters ending with a newline.

Left out: our suspend-to-RAM firmware stop (g16_deep_sleep, its
publish hook and sleep policy) and the PMP vote release at the sleep's
commit, which belonged to the dropped s2r driver. A deep sleep runs
Aurora's G16 sleep path as carried by the sleep series.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
